      "message": "LGTM; \nOptional nit: since `results` is zero-initialized to `kNoCodeUnitFlag`, testing `U+1F600` (`[9, 13)`) with expected `kNoCodeUnitFlag` wouldn\u0027t catch a bug where bytes 10..12 weren\u0027t written. Using a 4-byte ideograph (e.g. U+20000 `\\xF0\\xA0\\x80\\x80` -\u003e `kIdeographic`) or a supplementary format control (e.g. U+1D173 `\\xF0\\x9D\\x85\\xB3` -\u003e `kControl`, which could also test the UTF-16 surrogate pair path `u\"\\uD834\\uDD73\"`) would assert non-zero flags across all 4 UTF-8 bytes / both UTF-16 surrogates.",
